{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180958-enfant-terrible-the-scion-origin-pc-thread","id":1180958,"title":"Enfant Terrible: The Scion Origin PC thread!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-30T18:28:14-08:00","id":1180958,"title":"Enfant Terrible: The Scion Origin PC thread!","content":"Ho ho ho! Scion: Origin is out, so lets make some Characters!<br /> <br /> (Note: Scion: Origin is the most foundational tome of the line, with Scion: Hero, Scion: Demigod and Scion: god going on top. Hence, characters made with Scion: Origin are basically Mortal+ and include Pre-visitation Scions, supernaturally empowered mortals or minor supernatural figures/supernatural figures at the beginning of their journey to divinity, like One tailed Kitsune)<br /> <br /> Since this is the first character, lets have a quick run through character creation. <br /> <br /> Step 1: Concept. - Every game has this, who is your character and what spark of life animates them?<br /> <br /> Hmm, something striking then, a splashy intro:<br /> <br /> Guo Er: Prince of the Walled City of Kowloon!<br /> <br /> <br /> Step 2: Paths. - You were someone before, who was that? How did you get here?<br /> <br /> Each path you choose allows you to pick three Abilities (by the way, this is the main source of your skills in game, so pick wisely), and depending on whether your Path is Primary, Secondary or Tertiary (denoting how important they are to you as a person), you get 3/2/1 points in the Abilities you picked (max 5 points in any ability, extra points can be put where you please)<br /> <br /> <br /> Origin Path: Beijing Opera Rafters Rat (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Abilities: Close Combat, Athletics, Persuasion (2 points in each)<br /> <br /> Hey, our rooftop rugrat is back.<br /> <br /> The little monkey, always copying our &quot;Monkey King&quot; rehearsals...<br /> <br /> Oi! Can the chatter you two, he makes the movements more accurately than you useless gossips ever could, all with no training! You shame your ancestors! Get going backstage!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> *sigh* If we had been a bit faster, we would have had you, Young Master Prodigy. But you just had to go catch the eye of the Sect Elder didn't you...<br /> <br /> <br /> Role Path: Rising star of the Sect (Primary)<br /> <br /> Abilities: Close Combat, Academics, Empathy (3 points in each)<br /> <br /> F\u00f9ny\u00echng Everyone! Welcome to the wonders of HK! I'm your host Melissa Ying, and tonight, one of Hong Kong's unsung heroes, the Sage of the Walled City!<br /> <br /> For most of the week, he's Guo Er, Esquire, son of Guo Men - the influential community organizer and head of the mysterious and extensive Mendicant Brotherhood. <br /> <br /> A gifted child, Guo Er rose quickly through the ranks of the Brotherhood, and today he is treasurer, legal advisor and chronicler of the august charitable and patriotic organization, but two days a week, as tradition demands, he dons rags and goes out into the walled city to beg for alms, living the life of a beggar. <br /> <br /> Only, not being content to be almost running one of Hong Kong's oldest and most benevolent charitable bodies, Guo Er uses this chance to do even more good! Look here! A serpentine line has formed around the block to where he hands out his pro-bono legal counsel to the poor and destitute of he walled city! <br /> <br /> Lets just cut to the head of the queue...<br /> <br /> Alms for the hungry...<br /> <br /> Master Guo, what drives you to do this manner of charity? You could be one of the most influential men of the city under 30 if you wanted?<br /> <br /> Ma'am, I'm a simple beggar, no &quot;Master&quot; as you call me. And no offence I'd be more than happy to talk to you, and maybe get to know you better later over lunch (your treat), but Widow Lan here has already paid me in boiled eggs and I really have to resolve this &quot;issue&quot; she has with some loansharks, so maybe later? *wink*<br /> <br /> Oh... oh my. Well there you have it viewers! The future of the Mendicant Brotherhood is in good hands!... anyone around here have a pen and some paper? I've errrmm, got to write my phone number down...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Pantheon Path (Shen): Equal of Heaven. (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Abilities: Academics (Required because of Shen), Leadership (Required because of Shen), Persuasion (1 point in each)<br /> <br /> ... And then after your election when we all started spitting on you, do you remember what he did? *hee ha ha!*<br /> <br /> He grabbed the Chief's staff and whupped three of you black and blue, if I recall..?<br /> <br /> *HA HA HA!* You should have seen your face then, Ah Men! There was such a commotion. How would a 10 year old know the secret Dog Beating Staff Technique passed only to the next Chief?<br /> <br /> ... Ironically, even though he's mastered the style, he hides it. Says he doesn't like the name. Do you know, he only saw me practice it the one time too, the night before the election. All our secrets laid bare before a child, now a pillar of our Sect.<br /> <br /> When are you going to put him forward as a candidate for the Chief position, Men? There'll be grousing about nepotism and other nonsense, but everyone knows he's the logical choice. Just let him prove himself in the ring. That'll shut the other Elders up. <br /> <br /> ... I don't even want to admit this to myself sometimes, but I have this feeling in my dan-tian that he's meant for bigger things...<br /> <br /> Abilities: (You get to pick a specialization for every one that is 3 points and over)<br /> <br /> Close Combat OOOOO (Dog Beating Staff Technique)<br /> Academics OOOO (Law)<br /> Persuasion OOO (Lets make a deal)<br /> Empathy OOO (Knowing Exactly what people want)<br /> Athletics OO<br /> Leadership O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T18:30:34-08:00","id":1180959,"title":"","content":"Step 4 (Step 2 and 3 were the origin paths and skills): Attributes<br /> <br /> There are 3 &quot;arenas&quot; (areas of ability) - Physical, Mental and Social<br /> <br /> Each arena has three &quot;Approaches&quot; - Force, Finesse and Resilience. How you solve problems<br /> <br /> How it works out in practice is like this:<br /> <br /> Physical Arena<br /> Might (Force)<br /> Dexterity (Finesse)<br /> Stamina (Resilience)<br /> <br /> Mental Arena<br /> Intellect (Force)<br /> Cunning (Finesse)<br /> Resolve (Resilience)<br /> <br /> Social Arena<br /> Presence (Force)<br /> Manipulation (Finesse)<br /> Composure (Resilience)<br /> <br /> Firstly all Attributes have a dot in them for free (no zero dot attributes), then you decide on your Character's main approach style, is he/she/ze forceful in everything? A cunning manipulator? Or a rock, unmoved by the waves? Your character's approach gets a bonus two dots.<br /> <br /> So, being the little monkey that he is, Guo Er favors finesse, so his attributes are (for now):<br /> <br /> Physical Arena<br /> Might (Force) O<br /> Dexterity (Finesse) OOO<br /> Stamina (Resilience) O<br /> <br /> Mental Arena<br /> Intellect (Force) O<br /> Cunning (Finesse) OOO<br /> Resolve (Resilience) O<br /> <br /> Social Arena<br /> Presence (Force) O<br /> Manipulation (Finesse) OOO<br /> Composure (Resilience) O<br /> <br /> Now you get to pick Primary (6 points) Secondary (4 points) Tertiary (2 Points) once again! Guo Er is a Social Primary, Physical Secondary, Mental Tertiary character.<br /> <br /> Physical Arena<br /> Might (Force) O<br /> Dexterity (Finesse) OOOOO<br /> Stamina (Resilience) OOO<br /> <br /> Having 3 points in Stamina gets you extra health levels later. 1 dot is human average. 5 is Human maximum.<br /> <br /> Mental Arena<br /> Intellect (Force) OO<br /> Cunning (Finesse) OOO<br /> Resolve (Resilience) OO<br /> <br /> Social Arena<br /> Presence (Force) OO<br /> Manipulation (Finesse) OOOOO<br /> Composure (Resilience) OOOO<br /> <br /> Step 5: Calling and Knacks<br /> <br /> This is basically a declaration of what kind of character you're going to be. Your superpowers (such as they are at the Origin level) come from here, and if you are a Pre-visitation Scion, you have to pick one that matches your Sire's character. (Loki gets trickster).<br /> <br /> Being a Scion of XXX XXXXXX of the Shen (its obvious, but a no prize for those of you who guess), Guo Er can pick from the Trickster (self evident), Liminal (you stand at the boundary of all things) and Warrior (your calling is conflict) Callings. <br /> <br /> Being a sort that is at the nexus of things, Guo Er choose the Liminal Calling. He will be the One who Stands in the Gap.<br /> <br /> He gets to pick three Knacks! (Supernatural Powers)<br /> <br /> Note: I know you should only get 1, but you get to pick up 2 later (or your Birthright items which we don't have any idea about so I picked Knacks).<br /> <br /> So I picked:<br /> <br /> Flatlander: In combat you get to do the following if you roll well enough:<br /> <br /> Glimpse the other Side - Send foes... Elsewhere... for a turn. Where? gods only know.<br /> Stutter Time - Opponents act in a turn slower.<br /> Bend Space - Reduce the Range of a target (Stopping bullets matrix style!)<br /> <br /> <br /> Neither the Minute or the Hour: Make a dire pronouncement (that can be complete Blarney if you want) about a target's death, your target suffers a +1 difficulty to all actions for 1 scene<br /> <br /> Unobtrusive Visitor: Wherever you are, you belong there, and it is right that you are there, listening to everything everyone says. <br /> <br /> Step 6: Odds and Ends.<br /> <br /> <br /> You also get an extra Attribute Point and 5 extra Skill points, I chose these:<br /> <br /> Physical Arena<br /> Might (Force) O<br /> Dexterity (Finesse) OOOOO<br /> Stamina (Resilience) OOO<br /> <br /> Mental Arena<br /> Intellect (Force) OO<br /> Cunning (Finesse) OOO<br /> Resolve (Resilience) OO<br /> <br /> Social Arena<br /> Presence (Force) OO<br /> Manipulation (Finesse) OOOOO<br /> Composure (Resilience) OOOOO (Extra point went here, Defence in combat is apparently based on Resilience Attributes, so I thought it a good investment)<br /> <br /> Skills<br /> Close Combat OOOOO (Dog Beating Staff Technique)<br /> Academics OOOOO (Law)<br /> Persuasion OOOOO (Lets make a deal)<br /> Empathy OOO (Knowing Exactly what people want)<br /> Athletics OOO (Footraces)<br /> Leadership O<br /> Subterfuge O <br /> <br /> Knacks<br /> Flatlander<br /> Unobtrusive visitor<br /> Neither the minute nor the hour<br /> <br /> And phew, Guo Er is done! Next maybe I'll do a non Pre-visitation Scion character.<br /> <br /> Things to ponder:<br /> <br /> 1. How do you decide what gear you have?<br /> 2. Can you close combat with Dexterity? (Most people say yes, some on the Onyx Path say no)<br /> 3. I suppose you can just nick the Knacks of the supernatural creatures?<br /> 4. Did I get everything right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:02:18-08:00","id":1180969,"title":"","content":"Clearly he's a Scion of Horse-Face. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That looks pretty cool. <br /> <br /> Regarding Paths, is there a list you pick from, or do you design your own?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:14:22-08:00","id":1180972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180958-enfant-terrible-the-scion-origin-pc-thread?p=1180969#post1180969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly he's a Scion of Horse-Face. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That looks pretty cool. <br /> <br /> Regarding Paths, is there a list you pick from, or do you design your own?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can design your own, but there are pre made ones to pick from.<br /> <br /> The Pantheon path is restrictive, 2/3 of the Skills are already picked for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:20:59-08:00","id":1180977,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks.<br /> <br /> It seems like you could easily do a cross-Pantheon chronicle involving PCs who all share the same or similar Origin (or possibly Role).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T00:57:50-08:00","id":1181037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1180958-enfant-terrible-the-scion-origin-pc-thread?p=1180977#post1180977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, thanks.<br /> <br /> It seems like you could easily do a cross-Pantheon chronicle involving PCs who all share the same or similar Origin (or possibly Role).</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s like the default campaign isn\u2019t it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T06:30:47-08:00","id":1181376,"title":"","content":"<b>Ichiro Bozu</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Paths</u></b><br /> <br /> Origin Path : Two Embers in a Honshuu Wasteland - The only one of his litter to surive, Ichiro, a Tanuki, was born under a waterlogged couch in a Honshuu tip, in the midst of the sprawling Japan suburbia. (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Skills: Survival, Subterfuge, Occult<br /> <br /> Role Path: Cheat of Cheats - Iichiro lies to live, he has no compunctions about that. But he picks his quarry carefully. Only one who has taken another for a fool, can truly be fooled themselves. (Primary)<br /> <br /> Skills: Empathy, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Supernatural Path: Bake-Danuki - As the legend of the virtuous liar grows, Ichiro finds himself getting drawn into the secret machinations of the great Kami themselves! Poor him, he's only ever wanted good sake and some Maguro sashimi to go with it. (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Skills: Occult (Bake Danuki), Culture (Bake Danuki), Persuasion<br /> <br /> <b><u>Skills (With final addition)</u></b><br /> Persuasion OOOOO (Have I got a deal for you!)<br /> Subterfuge OOOOO (I have a thousand faces)<br /> Empathy OOOOO (I know you're lying to me)<br /> Occult OOO (Hyakki Yakko)<br /> Culture OOO (Easy Familiarity)<br /> Survival OO<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attributes</u></b><br /> <br /> Finesse, of course.<br /> <br /> Physical (Tertiary)<br /> <br /> Strength O<br /> Dexterity OOO<br /> Stamina OOO<br /> <br /> Social (Primary)<br /> <br /> Presence OOO<br /> Manipulation OOOOO<br /> Composure OOO<br /> <br /> Mental (Secondary)<br /> <br /> Intellect O<br /> Cunning OOOO<br /> Resolve OOOOO (Very resolved to not die)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Knacks:</u></b><br /> <br /> Takes One to Know One (Trickster): You automatically know when you are being lied to or cheated.<br /> Set the Stage (Kitsune): A simple prop makes people believe whatever you wish about a certain place (a stethoscope turns a living room into a doctor's office. A wall diploma makes one a lawyer.)<br /> Dress for Success (Kitsune): Even the flimsiest of disguises convinces people that you are who you say you are.<br /> <br /> Query: Are you assumed to be able to do the leaf transformation thing innately, or do you need a knack for that too?<br /> <br /> Edit: Hmm, he should also have the fluffy tail thing or something similar (the drawback Kitsune have). In the case of Tanuki, I think its whenever their Legend grows, so do their balls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}